AltoConvexCreditLineMarket::setCreditAccount()
├── when caller is not owner
│   └── it should revert with OwnableUnauthorizedAccount
├── when new credit account is zero
│   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketZeroAddress
├── given current account has collateral but no debt
│   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketPositionNotEmpty without changing state
├── given current account has debt and collateral
│   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketPositionNotEmpty without changing state
├── given current account has debt but no collateral
│   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketPositionNotEmpty without changing state
├── given current account has no debt or collateral
│   ├── it should update creditAccount and emit SetCreditAccount with old and new addresses
│   ├── it should preserve rewardRecipient account-specific authorizations and market accounting
│   ├── it should allow the new account to add collateral borrow repay withdraw and set its reward recipient
│   ├── it should reject operations targeting the old credit account
│   ├── it should not grant the old account or its delegates authority over the new account
│   ├── it should allow rotation after full repayment and collateral withdrawal
│   ├── it should preserve bad debt and used capacity when rotating after foreclosure
│   ├── it should remain callable while paused frozen or Convex inactive
│   └── when new account equals current account
│       └── it should emit SetCreditAccount with the same address
└── when owner attempts rotation during a collateral transfer callback
    └── it should revert with ReentrancyGuardReentrantCall and roll back the withdrawal
